    <briefdescription>
<para>Indicates that the current GATT procedure was completed successfully or that it failed with an error. </para>
    </briefdescription>
    <detaileddescription>
<para>All GATT commands excluding <ref refid="group__sl__bt__gatt_1ga2fb8049cafc0efc9f06bf2fae7c3c119" kindref="member">sl_bt_gatt_write_characteristic_value_without_response</ref> and <ref refid="group__sl__bt__gatt_1ga691b8ffe8734ea853fe9315d0767db75" kindref="member">sl_bt_gatt_send_characteristic_confirmation</ref> will trigger this event. As a result, the application must wait for this event before issuing another GATT command (excluding the two aforementioned exceptions).</para>
<para><bold>Note:</bold> After a failed GATT procedure with SL_STATUS_TIMEOUT error, further GATT transactions over this connection are not allowed by the stack. </para>
    </detaileddescription>
